## Context
Audit: `conception/2026-10-29-memory-system-audit.md` (PR #1984) R2; Fable and GPT-6 Astra reviews of the fifth hoard (PR #1975, closed unmerged 2026-10-29 by author decision). Today a hoard reads only journal entries newer than the last accepted report and
appends to topics, so topics only grow. The fifth hoard's branch `hoard-2026-10-29` stays on the
forge as reference.

## Scope
- Each hoard re-derives every topic from the previous topic and the journal, writes it fresh
  under the caps of 1348, and reports the net byte change. A run that grows the store explains why.
- Pair with the existing second pass so a rewrite does not drop a caveat.
- Run the next harness hoard this way; it replaces the closed fifth hoard.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The hoard skill and HOARD.md describe the rebuild and the net-change report
- [ ] One harness hoard has run as a rebuild and was accepted by the author

## Input design: native memories as inboxes (author, 2026-10-29)
The author's idea was to merge the tools' memories. Accepted shape (option A): each runtime keeps
capturing in its native store; smelt drains the native stores and the journal into the
departments (1348); the repository store is canonical and the only one all four runtimes read.
Merging is smelt's input step, not a replacement for it.

Evidence (lair session probes, 2026-10-29, padme only; the reports were session scratch,
so the numbers are kept here):
- Claude Code native: 1,137 notes (1.9 MB) in 47 of 268 project dirs; types feedback 68%,
  project 15%, reference 8%, user 1%, untyped 9%. Tombstones (`# DELETED 2026-09-16`) 92;
  notes missing from their index 56; 290 notes (26%) in superseded, renamed or old-path dirs,
  including a 138-note store under `~/.claude`.
- Harness native store (27 notes), single coder: Commission 44%, rule in disguise 41%,
  unique (never in the repo) 52%, stale 22%, full duplicate 26%. AEDIST sample (25 live notes,
  about ±18 points): rule in disguise 64%, unique 68%, harness machinery stored in a project 44%.
- Cross-store contradictions: padme CPU (3945WX/12 cores versus 3975WX/32 cores); "no wait
  tickets" versus "a reminder is an open Blocked-by ticket"; `prose_edits_on_main` versus `rules/git.md`.
- Codex native memories: feature off, store empty (1346). Pi and Vibe: no built-in memory in the
  installed releases. Pi's ecosystem has many memory packages (pi.dev lists 219 under "memory";
  for example `pi-claude-memory`, `@fractaal/pi-cross-agent-memory`, `@getpipher/armory-memory`
  import, `pi-codex-memory`, `pi-agent-memory-repo`). They merge stores, but none verifies,
  retires or budgets: that part is smelt's.

Drain requirements:
- Read the directory, not the index; skip tombstones; parse the nested `metadata.type`;
  ignore mtimes, since they are bulk-touched.
- Map stores to repositories by the repository, not the cwd: resolve old paths and aliases
  (`.project-aliases.json` has 14) and route harness machinery found in a project store to the harness.
- Batch by store; the first full drain is about 480k tokens (an estimate).
- Commission receives author rulings (the largest flow). Notes that prescribe behaviour are filed
  as rulings, never promoted to rules; 1351 lists them as candidates.
- A time-limited note gets a revisit date (for example, the main-guard watch ends 2026-11-03).
- A drained native note is emptied, or its index points to the department page; pick one, and
  measure with 1346 that Claude Code then reads it.

## Imagine (raid d2253c)
- Premise check: the skill was renamed hoard to smelt on 2026-10-29 (a1dbb4b8): the ticket's "hoard skill and HOARD.md" are now skills/smelt/SKILL.md and memory/SMELT.md (prompt v8-r3, 1348 landed caps and the topic job, af95a78f). No contrary change: SMELT.md still says "reads entries not yet covered" and "Consolidate" prunes/merges in place, so the delta behaviour the ticket targets is intact. PREMISE OBJECTION: no. Wording in the ticket is stale only.
- Current state: 11 topics, several far over 4 KB (raid-review-and-merge 21 KB, runtime-observations 9.4 KB); 1348 set caps but did not shrink pages. A rebuild is the first thing that makes them comply.
- Simplest path: edit the prompt and skill so the run re-derives each topic from prior topic plus journal (new SMELT.md section "Rebuild", revision v8-r4), add a "Net change" report line (bytes before/after per topic, reason if the store grows), state that pass two checks each dropped caveat against the previous page. Extend scripts/memory_sizes.py minimally to print before/after (git ref) so the net figure is measured, not hand-derived.
- YAGNI: skip the native-store drain (input design section, 480k tokens, mapping aliases); it is a separate scope and not in Scope or Exit criteria. Named narrowing: criteria untouched, drain is out of this PR.
- D1: criterion 2 needs a real smelt run on this repo plus author acceptance (real spend, author-gated). The raid can deliver criterion 1 and launch the run, but cannot close the ticket. Recommend: PR closes criterion 1 only, run separate.
- D2: the Commission page (pinned rulings never cut) and the pinned tie-break: rebuild must carry pinned lines verbatim; confirm the net-change report counts them.
- D3: bump the prompt revision to v8-r4 or keep v8-r3; tests/test_smelt_migrate.py and test_memory_v8_pilot.py pin v8-r3 (grep to confirm); recommend v8-r4 and update the pins.
- D4: do net-change numbers belong in the helper or only in the report? Recommend the helper (one command, reproducible).
- Price: 2-3 coder-hours for the doc, helper and tests; the rebuild run about 1 hour of agent time, roughly 480k tokens only if the drain were included (it is not). Not a monster: 4-6 files, no shared symbol, but one sign-off unit needs author acceptance.

## Plan (raid d2253c)
- 1. tests first: add to tests/test_dream_v8.py a test that SMELT.md has a "Rebuild" section stating topics are re-derived and a "Net change" report line, and that SKILL.md says the same (fails today: neither text exists; a wrong implementation that only touches one file is caught by checking both). Add a scripts/memory_sizes.py test comparing two topic dirs: fixture page grows 3000 to 5000 bytes, expects net +2000 and a reason-required flag; a wrong implementation that sums only the after side fails.
- 2. memory/SMELT.md: new "Rebuild" section after Read (~line 38) and "Net change" item in Report (~line 150); revision line 3 to v8-r4; change "not yet covered" wording in Read item 1 so topics are rebuilt from the prior page plus all journal evidence, accepted reports stay as ledger. Second pass line: re-examine each caveat of the previous page, none dropped without a Retired line.
- 3. skills/smelt/SKILL.md: Procedure step 2 (~line 107) say rebuild not append; step 3 add the net-change report line; Three main functions unchanged.
- 4. scripts/memory_sizes.py: add --before REF/dir net-change output; main(topics_dir) signature kept.
- 5. Update revision pins in tests/test_smelt_migrate.py and tests/test_memory_v8_pilot.py if D3 = v8-r4; run make skills-catalog if the description changes (it should not).
- 6. After merge, run /smelt on this repo (criterion 2), author accepts.
- Dependencies: none on 1346, 1355, 1358, 1360-1363; 1351 (brood, lists rulings) reads Commission but does not conflict; PR #2013 files are disjoint.
- Files touched: memory/SMELT.md, skills/smelt/SKILL.md, scripts/memory_sizes.py, tests/test_dream_v8.py, tests/test_smelt_migrate.py, tests/test_memory_v8_pilot.py, tests/test_memory_sizes.py (new or existing), tickets/1349 file.

## Orchestrator decisions (raid d2253c)
- The PR delivers exit criterion 1 only and does not close the ticket; criterion 2 (a real harness smelt run as a rebuild, accepted by the author) stays open.
- D2 yes: pinned Commission rulings carried verbatim and counted in the net change. D3 yes: bump to v8-r4, update the pins. D4 yes: the helper measures the net change.

## Feasibility and blind spot (raid d2253c)
- Feasibility PASS; anchors drift (Read ends near SMELT.md:32, Procedure step 2 at :114).
- Blind spot: memory/journal is about 1.1 MB, about 275k tokens (derived at 4 bytes/token), above the 256K guard. The rebuild procedure must batch by department (journal episodes per topic, measured) so one run never holds the whole journal; measure bytes per topic before writing the prompt.
